      quiz: { q: 'Total cost C(Q) = Q²/2 + 8 (MC = Q) and market demand Q = 220 − 20P. Find the monopoly outcome, then the number of identical price-taking firms when the market price is 4.', parts: [['Monopoly output', 10], ['Monopoly price', 10.5], ['Monopoly profit', 47], ['Number of firms at P = 4', 35]], solution: ['MR = 11 − Q/10 = Q gives Q = 10 and P = 10.5; profit = 105 − 58 = 47.', 'At P = 4 each firm makes q = 4; market demand is 140, so there are 35 firms, each with zero economic profit.'] },
