      title: 'Adding a government and trade to the Keynesian cross',
      question: 'Utopia has C = 20 + 0.8Y and I = 80, with no government or trade. (a) Find the multiplier and equilibrium income. (b) A government sets an income tax of t = 0.25 and spends G = 100; the economy exports 30 and its marginal propensity to import is 0.1. Find the new multiplier and income. (c) Find the budget balance and the trade balance. (d) If investment does not depend on the interest rate, how effective is monetary policy?',
